{"availability":"available","full":"authzed/spicedb","name":"spicedb","description":"Open Source, Google Zanzibar-inspired database for scalably storing and querying fine-grained authorization data","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":7116,"forks":429,"created":"2021-08-16T15:32:09Z","updated":"2026-10-02T21:40:51Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://authzed.com/docs","topics":["abac","acl","authorization","ciam","cloud-native","database","distributed-systems","entitlements","fga","fine-grained-access-control","fine-grained-authorization","kubernetes","permissions","rbac","rebac","security","security-tools","zanzibar"],"demo":null,"color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:34.894Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:34.894Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:34.894Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:19:34.894Z","stars":7116,"forks":429}],"technologies":["Go"],"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:37.515Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SpiceDB is the most mature open source project inspired by Google's internal authorization system: [Zanzibar].","As of 2021, broken access control became the #1 threat to web security according to OWASP. With SpiceDB, platform and product teams can be be protected by answering this question easily: \"can subject X perform action Y on resource Z?\"","Similar to a relational database, developers define a schema, write data in the form of relationships, and then use SpiceDB's clients to issue permission checks in their application to determine what actions a user can take on a resource. Other queries are also possible, such as \"What can subject do?\" or \"Who can access resource?\"."],"features":["World-class engineering: painstakingly built by experts that pioneered the cloud-native ecosystem","Authentic design: mature and feature-complete implementation of Google's Zanzibar paper","Proven in production: 5ms p95 when scaled to millions of queries/s, billions of relationships","Global consistency: consistency configured per-request unlocks correctness while maintaining performance","Multi-paradigm: caveated relationships combine the best concepts in authorization: ABAC & ReBAC"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/authzed/spicedb/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e1b36839da8a57698fdca543cd0a65c1d5141de17adce2fb334e6d19a37c7803","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:15:53.892Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:37.509Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-02T21:40:51Z","enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T07:02:19.420Z","latestRelease":{"name":"v1.56.2","tag":"v1.56.2","publishedAt":"2026-09-11T18:01:43Z","url":"https://github.com/authzed/spicedb/releases/tag/v1.56.2"},"releaseCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T07:02:19.420Z","screenshots":[],"projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"SpiceDB is the most mature open source project inspired by Google's internal authorization system: [Zanzibar].","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/authzed/spicedb/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"You can choose to self-host SpiceDB, or use [AuthZed Cloud], a fully managed service.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/authzed/spicedb/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"optional","text":"If you choose to self-host, we recommend deploying SpiceDB using Kubernetes.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/authzed/spicedb/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"e1b36839da8a57698fdca543cd0a65c1d5141de17adce2fb334e6d19a37c7803","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/authzed/spicedb/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:37.509Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/authzed/spicedb/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:37.510Z","hash":"e1b36839da8a57698fdca543cd0a65c1d5141de17adce2fb334e6d19a37c7803","originalBytes":19436,"storedBytes":19436,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["spicedb","authzed","community","google","alt","authoriza